course: dictionary
lesson: 2477
title: Words for time of day
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a time of day, and the words around them tell you which time. «It's no sort of night for bed anyhow, daybreak is not far off» says the Rat. The night is nearly over, so daybreak must be the time just before morning.
explain: Check your guess by swapping in a meaning. If daybreak means the time when light first appears, the sentence still makes sense: the sky will soon be light and the night will be over. Phrases such as «before daybreak» and «from daybreak till dusk» show you where daybreak sits in the day.
fact: Daybreak is a noun, a word for a time you can name.
fact: «Daybreak» means the time in the early morning when light first appears in the sky.
fact: «Daybreak» means the same as dawn.
fact: Useful phrases: «at daybreak», «before daybreak», «from daybreak till dusk».
fact: In science, daybreak links to sunrise and to the Earth turning.
exercise: «Daybreak is not far off», the Rat says. What does daybreak mean? | *The time when light first appears in the early morning | The time the sun goes down | The middle of the night | A kind of bird
exercise: Which word means the same as daybreak? | midnight | *dawn | dusk | noon
exercise: The Mole and the Rat will not go to bed. Why not? | It is already noon | They are not tired at all | They have lost Portly | *Daybreak is near, so the night is nearly over
test: «He set off at daybreak to catch the train.» When did he set off? | At noon | At midnight | At dusk | *Early in the morning, as the light appeared
test: Which phrase means from the first light of morning until evening? | at midnight | from noon till midnight | before daybreak | *from daybreak till dusk
exam: Which sentence uses daybreak correctly? | We ate our supper at daybreak. | The shop closed at daybreak. | The sun went down at daybreak. | *The birds began to sing at daybreak, as the sky turned pale.
